From 02b97165e1fd299cda0d66803a45edd98b272256 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miroslav=20Mr=C3=A1z?= <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 22:53:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] media: venus: hfi_msgs: parse IRIS1 firmware version
 string
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Venus firmware on the SM7150 reports its version as
"14:VIDEO.IR.1.2-00053-PROD-1", which none of the existing sscanf patterns
match, so the version was left unparsed. Add a fourth pattern for the
"14:VIDEO.IR.%u.%u-%u" form and, when nothing matches, print the
unrecognized string in the error path to ease bring-up of future firmware.

Signed-off-by: Miroslav Mráz <mraz.miro@seznam.cz>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c
index 47b99d5b5af7..537e0dc45e57 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/hfi_msgs.c
@@ -321,7 +321,13 @@ sys_get_prop_image_version(struct venus_core *core,
 	if (ret)
 		goto done;
 
-	dev_err(dev, VDBGL "error reading F/W version\n");
+	ret = sscanf(img_ver, "14:VIDEO.IR.%u.%u-%u",
+		     &core->venus_ver.major, &core->venus_ver.minor, &core->venus_ver.rev);
+	if (ret)
+		goto done;
+
+	dev_err(dev, VDBGL "error reading F/W version (str: %.*s)\n",
+		VER_STR_SZ, img_ver);
 	return;
 
 done:
